{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 7, :comments ["<b>And Elohim made the firmament.</b> He set it firm upon its stand — and that is its 'making', as in ״וְעָשְׂתָה אֶת צִפָּרְנֶיהָ״ (Deuteronomy 21)." "<b>From above the firmament.</b> Concerning the firmament it says only מֵעַל לָרָקִיעַ, because they are suspended in the air. And for what reason was כִּי טוֹב not said on the second day? Because the work of the waters was not completed until the third day, and He began it on the second — and something not completed is not in its fullness and goodness. And on the third, when the work of the waters was completed and He began and completed another work, He doubled in it כִּי טוֹב twice — once for the completion of the second day's work and once for the completion of the day's work."], :book :genesis, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 1, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:57:03.850734682Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}